The key distinction for this library

Just like postpartum, I would not build:

❌ Men's Health After 40
❌ Dad-Bod Transformation
❌ Fitness for Men 40+
❌ Men's Grooming 40+
❌ Men's Confidence After 40
❌ Midlife Reinvention

Those are domains, not sufficiently scoped products.

Instead:

"I can't play football with my son anymore."

"My trousers don't fit and my daughter's wedding is in six weeks."

"I haven't entered a gym in ten years and I'm embarrassed to start again."

"I keep crashing at 3PM and I'm relying on coffee to finish work."

"My children are almost grown and I suddenly realize I have no idea who I am outside being their father."

"I'm divorced at 47 and haven't dated since my 20s."

Those are situations.

And then we build the transformation around the situation—not the other way around.

That is the same principle we established for the Postpartum library, and I think it is even more important for Men's Health & Reinvention 40+, because the broad market is saturated with generic "get fit after 40" advice. The hidden opportunity is in the specific life moments that make a 40+ man finally care enough to change.